<title>THAILAND: Thailand suspends sugar production at two mills.</title>
<headline>Thailand suspends sugar production at two mills.</headline>
<dateline>BANGKOK 1997-03-18</dateline>
<text>
<p>The Thai Cane and Sugar Board on Tuesday suspended production at the Nong Yai and Ang Wian sugar mills for making raw sugar without government permission.  </p>
<p>Both sugar mills have licences to produce only brown sugar, a senior board official told Reuters.</p>
<p>&quot;We seized their raw sugar and suspended the production of raw sugar. But they can continue producing brown sugar,&quot; she said.</p>
<p>The two sugar mills, with a crushing capacity of between 2,000 and 4,000 tonnes of sugar cane per day each, are located in the eastern province of Chonburi.</p>
<p>Thailand has 46 registered sugar mills.</p>
<p>-- Bangkok newsroom (662) 652-0642</p>
